{
  "_about": "The 17 distinct domain patterns of canon 0.36.0 (atip/1 1.4) that listed white space by hand, as `canon schema` printed them, with the 59 places that declared them. canon-0-37-claim-1-5 (`atip.claim15.04`) holds the 1.5 patterns of those places to these: the same values in and out. `canon-0-37-option-values` re-baselined it in one way: the 17 places of `changedBy037` (the six name and sentence options) are held to the text rule of that change (`atip.optionvalues.*`), not to these patterns, because that change deliberately narrows what they accept (a control character or a line break inside, an empty or blank value) and widens what the parser takes (the white space around). `canon-0-37-option-forms` re-baselined it in one more way: the 13 places of `changedBy037Forms` (the time options and the provider list) are held to the RFC 3339 and exact-name patterns of that change (`atip.optionforms.11`), which name no white space, because it deliberately refuses what they took (white space, a one-digit month, a sign on the year, a date alone for `--approval-at`, a capital in a name). The patterns and places stay here as the record of what 0.36.0 took, and `atip/option_values_0_36.json` and `atip/option_forms_0_36.json` list the values per class. `canon-0-38-provider-option` re-baselined it once more: `--providers` is not an option of any command in 0.38 (the repeatable `--harness` and `--no-harness` took its place), so its two places are listed under `changedBy038` and are no longer declared patterns to hold to anything; the 13 places of `changedBy037Forms` are 11 now.",
